              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argue that appellate precedent holds that plaintiffs who obtain a preliminary injunction are prevailing parties entitled to attorney's fees."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4981c3b5eb6c16713c8bcc0f03c45df7bf8f8e070e9cdb4f98aa9cdce58729fd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4981c3b5eb6c-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Millett, they further contend that fee entitlement is tied to a violation of Federal law, but a consent decree situation can also permit fees when the defendant does not resist final relief."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "United States",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4981c3b5eb6c16713c8bcc0f03c45df7bf8f8e070e9cdb4f98aa9cdce58729fd",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4981c3b5eb6c-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 18,
                "start": 18
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States, they note that a preliminary injunction does not itself determine a violation of Federal law."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
